Pill Engine - Licensing
=======================

Copyright (c) Mateusz Szymoński and the Pill Engine contributors.

Pill Engine is free for everyone who builds with it, from a solo developer
to a large studio, and it grows through what its community gives back. It
is offered under three alternative licensing routes. Choose the one that
fits you; you need only one, and the conditions of one never apply to
someone using another, except obligations already taken on under it.
Commercial use is allowed under all three. A "User Project" is anything
built with Pill Engine: a game, simulation, visualization or other
application.

1. Community License - legal/licenses/COMMUNITY_LICENSE.md
   Free for everyone, for commercial User Projects too, and your own code
   always stays private. Your changes to the engine (Pill Engine
   Modifications) may stay private below USD 300,000 Annual Revenue; once
   you grow past it, you are required to share them with the community
   (after a 6-month transition), or switch to the Open Source License or a
   Partner License.
   No forks or standalone engines. Source-available, not OSI-approved open
   source.

2. Open Source License - legal/licenses/LGPL-3.0_LICENSE.txt
   SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-only
   Free for everyone, with no revenue limit, for proprietary User Projects
   too. When you distribute a User Project, its recipients get Pill
   Engine's source, including your Pill Engine Modifications, and the means
   to relink it (LGPLv3 section 4). The included GPLv3 is part of the LGPLv3,
   not a separate option.

3. Partner License - legal/licenses/PARTNER_LICENSE.md
   A paid agreement with the Licensor for keeping Pill Engine Modifications
   private at any revenue, without the Community License's publishing duty, for
   the code it covers. Partner funding supports the further development of Pill
   Engine, so it benefits both sides: partners get a stronger engine to build
   on, and the community gets an engine that stays free for everyone. Today it
   goes to the Licensor; in the future, to a non-profit foundation for Pill
   Engine, independent of any company, once that foundation exists (see
   legal/GOVERNANCE.md). The Partner License is always a choice, never a
   requirement, includes no support or maintenance, and exists only once signed
   by both parties.

Third-party components keep their own licenses (see
legal/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md), which none of these licensing routes
overrides.

This file is only a summary. If it differs from the full text of the license
you choose, the full text applies.
